    <h2>Why We Built It</h2>
    <p>
      Most online 401(k) calculators still use outdated limits, round up to $980.77 × 26 (which exceeds $25,500), ignore 27-paycheck years, or bundle noisy 30-year retirement projections. This tool focuses strictly on getting your 2027 per-paycheck deferral right—including midyear job changes, ages 60–63 super catch-up, the $155,000 mandatory Roth catch-up rule, and employer match true-up risk.
    </p>

